    "title": "How to watch the Masters today, Round 4 start time, TV schedule",
    "text": "April 12, 2026, 10:30 a.m. ETIf the final round is anything like the third round, we're in for a wild ride Sunday at the 2026 Masters.Rory McIlroy and Cameron Young share the lead entering the last day of competition, with a host of big names within striking distance, all looking to secure a Green Jacket and become immortalized as a Masters champion.Below, you'll find everything you need to know about Sunday's final round of the Masters, including TV and streaming information, tee times and betting odds.What channel is the Masters on today? Time, TV scheduleAll times EasternParamount+ (12-2 p.m.) | CBS (2-7 p.m.)Coverage of the 2026 Masters final round will begin Sunday at 12 p.m. ET on Paramount+ before moving to CBS at 2 p.m. until the end of play. You can stream the CBS broadcast on Paramount+ or Fubo, which includes a free trial for new subscribers.Where to watch 2026 Masters on streamingHere's a look at the Masters final round alternate feeds streaming on Sunday:All times EasternOn the Range (10 a.m.-12 p.m.)CBS Sports Network, Paramount+, Masters AppFeatured groups (10:15 a.m.-7 p.m.)Paramount+, ESPN App, Prime Video, DirecTV, Masters AppHoles 4, 5 and 6 (10 a.m.-3:30 p.m.)Paramount+, ESPN App, Prime Video, DirecTV, Masters AppAmen Corner (11:45 a.m.-6 p.m.)Paramount+, ESPN App, Prime Video, DirecTV, Masters AppInside Amen Corner (11:45 a.m.-6 p.m.)Prime Video, Masters AppHoles 15 and 16 (Holes 15 & 16)Paramount+, ESPN App, Prime Video, DirecTV, Masters AppMasters tee times todayRory McIlroy and Cameron Young tee off in the final pairing at 2:25 p.m. ET on Sunday. Check out the full tee sheet here.Masters final round betting oddsRory McIlroy is the slight favorite to win his second straight Masters title Sunday. See the full list of odds here.We occasionally recommend interesting products and services. If you make a purchase by clicking one of the links, we may earn an affiliate fee. USA TODAY Network newsrooms operate independently, though, and this doesn’t influence our coverage.",
